    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.git\n\n### Description\n\nAs a user, I would like to be able to process the output of any command. Currently, some commands are displayed in the split (MiniGitCommandSplit), while others are displayed as notifications.\r\n\r\n**My use case**\r\n- I would like to display the list of branches in the buffer\r\n- Having this, I can set some nice mappings for this buffer to perform different operations with the branches (log, delete, etc.)\r\nNotification is useless for me in this context.\r\n\r\nPlease add some API to set callbacks for any command.",
