            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n> * I would like to display the list of branches in the buffer\r\n> \r\n> * Having this, I can set some nice mappings for this buffer to perform different operations with the branches (log, delete, etc.)\r\n>   Notification is useless for me in this context.\r\n\r\nForcing output appear in a split can be done [by explicitly using dedicated command modifiers](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-git.txt#L151-L153). For example: `:horizontal Git branch -a` or `:vertical Git branch -a`.\r\n\r\nWhich command is shown with `vim.notify()` and which in a split is [decided automatically based on information `git` itself provides](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-git.txt#L144-L149).\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nAs per the title (\"Add some API to get the output of any command in mini.git\"). The main point of 'mini.git' `:Git` command is for interactive usage. For any scripting/automation I'd recommend using Git CLI directly (with something like `vim.system`).\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
